    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vīcētĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vīcentĭa</span></b> ), ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town in</i> Gallia Transpadana, <i>in the
				territory of Venetia</i>, now <i>Vicenza</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tac. H.
				3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram. 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 5152</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 19,
				23, § 132</span></i>. —<i>Its
				inhabitants</i> are called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vīcētīni</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vīcentīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., Brut. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				11, 19, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 5, 4, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 14, 4</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3110</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(VEICETINI),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 3219</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">VICENTIN,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 5972</span></i>
			.</div>
